WEBVTT

00:01:38.233 --> 00:01:39.530
Damn it.

00:02:25.781 --> 00:02:28.443
Why are you doing this to me?

00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:31.714
Why do I have to die?

00:02:31.787 --> 00:02:34.688
I'm not alone.

00:02:34.756 --> 00:02:36.690
I'm not...

00:02:38.427 --> 00:02:39.894
Don't you...

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:12.426
The victim was Lavinia Whately,
age 24, a dancer...

00:03:12.494 --> 00:03:14.519
and she's a Third.

00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:23.835
How many humanoids
are there in this town?

00:03:23.905 --> 00:03:27.170
Sylibus. Detective Sylibus!

00:03:27.242 --> 00:03:28.402
Yes, sir?

00:03:28.477 --> 00:03:31.969
Is that terrorist D'anclaude
in Shinora?

00:03:32.047 --> 00:03:35.448
Yes. He's still in ICU.

00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:38.111
He's still unconscious.

00:03:38.186 --> 00:03:40.780
Besides, he has
round-the-clock security.

00:03:40.856 --> 00:03:43.290
The Shinora
police hospital, huh?

00:03:43.358 --> 00:03:47.852
That means
he has an accomplice.

00:03:47.929 --> 00:03:51.695
Well, we can't question him
in his condition.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.133
She worked him over good,
didn't she?

00:03:59.474 --> 00:04:02.204
I wonder just where
Armitage has gone.

00:04:07.883 --> 00:04:11.375
Why have all the Thirds
been female so far?

00:04:11.453 --> 00:04:12.818
Lowell...

00:04:12.888 --> 00:04:14.412
do you have
any new information?

00:04:25.867 --> 00:04:28.563
Yeah, that's right.
I'm a monster.

00:04:28.637 --> 00:04:30.332
What are you gonna do?

00:04:30.405 --> 00:04:32.737
You're gonna destroy me
or what?

00:04:32.808 --> 00:04:35.333
They blame us for recessions
and social problems.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.811
If humans don't want us,
why did they make us?

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.480
The first five
humanoid cadavers...

00:04:44.553 --> 00:04:48.148
were illegally manufactured.

00:04:48.223 --> 00:04:52.023
It is hard to analyze them
at our labs.

00:04:52.093 --> 00:04:54.027
Therefore they've been sent
to a lab...

00:04:54.095 --> 00:04:56.859
at the Conception Company
to be analyzed.

00:04:56.932 --> 00:04:58.126
But...

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.896
But they haven't turned up
any preliminary findings yet?

00:05:00.969 --> 00:05:03.369
No. I think they are too slow.

00:05:05.273 --> 00:05:08.208
I want to discuss with you
about the sixth cadaver later.

00:05:08.276 --> 00:05:09.868
Uh... yes, sir.

00:05:09.945 --> 00:05:13.312
And, Ross, I have something
I want to talk to you about.

00:05:13.381 --> 00:05:15.349
Come to my office later.

00:05:15.417 --> 00:05:16.577
Yes.

00:05:21.289 --> 00:05:23.985
Armitage carries
a Special A Class license.

00:05:25.961 --> 00:05:28.725
But she chose to become a cop.

00:05:28.797 --> 00:05:31.857
Do you understand
what I'm getting at?

00:05:31.933 --> 00:05:33.025
Yes.

00:05:33.101 --> 00:05:36.696
If the reason she disappeared
is because of you...

00:05:36.771 --> 00:05:39.137
You can interrogate me
all you want.

00:05:39.207 --> 00:05:40.139
I'm used to it.

00:05:40.208 --> 00:05:42.403
That won't be necessary.

00:05:42.477 --> 00:05:44.570
If you say
you don't know anything...

00:05:44.646 --> 00:05:46.113
that's good enough for me.

00:05:46.181 --> 00:05:47.739
Just one thing...

00:05:47.816 --> 00:05:49.909
you can ignore
what I'm going to say...

00:05:49.985 --> 00:05:51.213
but I have a hunch that...

00:05:51.286 --> 00:05:54.744
there's some kind of connection
between Armitage and...

00:05:54.823 --> 00:05:56.950
the killing of the Third types.

00:05:59.995 --> 00:06:01.758
Well, forget what I just said.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.765
If an officer is rumored
to be a humanoid...

00:06:04.833 --> 00:06:06.960
I have to quit MPD.

00:06:08.003 --> 00:06:10.836
Armitage was a great cop.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.919
Always hurts like hell
when the rain comes.

00:07:10.365 --> 00:07:11.992
Message.

00:07:12.067 --> 00:07:13.659
Where are you?

00:07:13.735 --> 00:07:17.831
We're partners, aren't we?

00:07:17.906 --> 00:07:21.706
The lieutenant suspects
you're a Third.

00:07:21.776 --> 00:07:23.835
It appears D'anclaude
is working with someone...

00:07:23.912 --> 00:07:26.813
because Thirds
are being murdered.

00:07:26.881 --> 00:07:29.349
Aren't you angry?

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:41.351
It appears D'anclaude
is working with someone...

00:07:41.429 --> 00:07:44.660
because Thirds
are being murdered.

00:07:44.733 --> 00:07:46.701
Aren't you angry?

00:07:46.768 --> 00:07:49.566
Come back, O. K?

00:08:08.523 --> 00:08:11.083
Good evening, Mademoiselle.

00:08:12.427 --> 00:08:16.386
Can you spare 10 credits...

00:08:16.464 --> 00:08:22.096
so this poor soul could enjoy
real beer from Earth?

00:08:25.807 --> 00:08:29.573
Now, behave, all right?

00:08:29.644 --> 00:08:34.047
Do you know someone
who writes novels around here?

00:08:37.485 --> 00:08:41.979
I myself used to be a writer
of fine on-line porno.

00:08:42.057 --> 00:08:45.618
They've never been published
in paperback, though.

00:09:23.865 --> 00:09:25.856
You'd better not move.

00:09:28.369 --> 00:09:31.270
I'm so sorry! Let go!

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:37.705
Now then, will you answer
my question, Mister?

00:09:37.779 --> 00:09:40.839
I will!
I will answer anything!

00:09:48.323 --> 00:09:53.659
Now, are you gonna
answer my question?

00:09:53.728 --> 00:09:56.196
Y-You're a monster!

00:10:05.874 --> 00:10:08.775
You've got an appointment
set up at Conception.

00:10:08.843 --> 00:10:10.902
You'll see Allen.
He's in charge.

00:10:10.979 --> 00:10:12.708
O.K. I'll get
on my way right now.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:16.079
Oh, yeah. Armitage was...

00:10:16.151 --> 00:10:20.679
communicating a lot
just before she vamoosed.

00:10:20.755 --> 00:10:23.451
I came across a log
in our memory bank.

00:10:23.525 --> 00:10:25.322
What? Who was it with?

00:10:25.393 --> 00:10:28.123
Can't tell you yet.
It's in machine language.

00:10:28.196 --> 00:10:30.187
I'll have to try
reverse computations first.

00:10:30.265 --> 00:10:31.562
Is it a code?

00:10:31.633 --> 00:10:33.999
I'm good at this kind of thing.

00:10:34.068 --> 00:10:36.195
Trust me. I'll decipher it.

00:10:36.271 --> 00:10:37.465
Thanks.

00:10:56.925 --> 00:11:00.292
You're Detective Sylibus
from MPD?

00:11:00.361 --> 00:11:03.159
Thanks for fitting me in today.

00:11:07.101 --> 00:11:09.695
I'm Allen,
V.P. Of Public Relations.

00:11:09.771 --> 00:11:11.966
Please have a seat.

00:11:13.808 --> 00:11:16.743
I'm here to discuss
the examination reports...

00:11:16.811 --> 00:11:18.642
on the Thirds we've requested.

00:11:18.713 --> 00:11:21.580
Ah, yes, we're working on it.

00:11:21.649 --> 00:11:27.747
The architecture of the type
is different from our designs...

00:11:27.822 --> 00:11:29.619
so it's taking some time.

00:11:29.691 --> 00:11:32.091
Even so, we need to...

00:11:34.662 --> 00:11:39.565
Could AL androids
composed of organic fibers...

00:11:39.634 --> 00:11:42.762
be an attractive product
for you?

00:11:42.837 --> 00:11:43.861
For what?

00:11:43.938 --> 00:11:46.998
What purpose do we serve
by simulating humans?

00:11:47.075 --> 00:11:49.441
Are you familiar with our motto?

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.444
"Home Robotization."

00:11:51.512 --> 00:11:54.948
But this is only under
the current legal system.

00:11:55.016 --> 00:11:57.951
It's natural for you
to try to recapture...

00:11:58.019 --> 00:12:01.113
the largest market share
by setting new standards.

00:12:01.189 --> 00:12:03.623
I see. It sounds like
you're implying...

00:12:03.691 --> 00:12:05.090
that we're manufacturing Thirds.

00:12:05.159 --> 00:12:08.026
In addition... let's see.

00:12:08.096 --> 00:12:09.791
Wait a minute.

00:12:09.864 --> 00:12:13.800
Is an inventor named Asakura
on your staff?

00:12:13.868 --> 00:12:17.360
Asakura? I can't remember.

00:12:17.438 --> 00:12:20.407
Yes, he is.
I would like to see him.

00:12:20.475 --> 00:12:22.340
He quit.
- When?

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:25.311
Before I joined the company...

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:27.314
several years ago.

00:12:29.484 --> 00:12:30.781
I understand.

00:12:30.852 --> 00:12:33.150
You're welcome
to check employee files.

00:12:33.221 --> 00:12:35.712
Everything can be verified.

00:12:41.462 --> 00:12:44.659
Is she a sample of
"Home Robotization"?

00:12:44.732 --> 00:12:46.063
One purpose of robots...

00:12:46.134 --> 00:12:49.297
is to help turn human fantasies
into reality, isn't it?

00:12:51.406 --> 00:12:56.639
They can do anything
except reproduce, right?

00:12:56.711 --> 00:13:00.545
Well, something like that.

00:13:06.421 --> 00:13:09.584
Drive home safely.

00:13:43.057 --> 00:13:45.025
Sorry to take up your time.

00:13:45.093 --> 00:13:46.458
No problem.

00:13:46.527 --> 00:13:49.462
Drive home safely now.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.328
Human fantasy!

00:14:13.821 --> 00:14:15.914
Personnel code copy.

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:18.458
The command is not authorized.

00:14:21.329 --> 00:14:22.728
Personnel code copy.

00:14:22.797 --> 00:14:25.095
Access wild, Third type.

00:14:25.166 --> 00:14:27.930
No data
on Third type located.

00:14:28.002 --> 00:14:29.936
Access wild, Asakura.

00:14:30.004 --> 00:14:33.167
Data on Asakura is locked.

00:14:33.241 --> 00:14:34.469
Close.

00:14:37.311 --> 00:14:40.246
I guess the information
is classified even to VPs.

00:14:53.861 --> 00:14:57.627
It's terrible!
This makes number seven.

00:14:57.698 --> 00:14:59.791
Seven dead Thirds.

00:14:59.867 --> 00:15:03.428
I can think of two people
who kill robots like this.

00:15:04.806 --> 00:15:08.207
I'm talking about D'anclaude
and Armitage.

00:15:08.276 --> 00:15:09.470
What's that?

00:15:09.544 --> 00:15:11.136
She told me before.

00:15:11.212 --> 00:15:14.181
She pities the robots
used for crime...

00:15:14.248 --> 00:15:16.978
so she kills them instantly.

00:15:17.051 --> 00:15:18.882
Still, it's unbelievable.

00:15:22.824 --> 00:15:25.987
Yeah, the village is a pit,
you know...

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:28.255
so I moved here
in the new downtown.

00:15:28.329 --> 00:15:32.595
Listen, I'd better
go back to writing.

00:15:36.037 --> 00:15:37.470
Writing.

00:15:37.538 --> 00:15:40.302
Continue. Untitled.

00:15:43.177 --> 00:15:44.610
Chapter 2, paragraph 5.

00:15:44.679 --> 00:15:50.345
"How could she greet the ones
from the deep far away?

00:15:50.418 --> 00:15:53.444
"She, who has spent a pleasant
and enchanting afternoon...

00:15:53.521 --> 00:15:57.082
"had never thought
about the person from Luluie...

00:15:57.158 --> 00:16:00.855
the same one who had
once picked her up here."

00:16:00.928 --> 00:16:02.953
Let's see.

00:16:16.577 --> 00:16:22.880
"Her battle
with the old gods ended.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:25.350
"As a spiritual truce
was struck...

00:16:26.587 --> 00:16:27.554
Who's there?

00:16:29.957 --> 00:16:31.254
Who are you?

00:16:34.729 --> 00:16:37.596
Armitage? Are you the one
who contacted me?

00:16:37.665 --> 00:16:38.825
You fooled me!

00:17:05.393 --> 00:17:07.827
You mean Armitage is a suspect?

00:17:07.895 --> 00:17:09.920
I wish I could deny it...

00:17:09.997 --> 00:17:12.056
but the woman's last words
said it all.

00:17:12.133 --> 00:17:16.729
The lieutenant had suspicions
about Armitage all along.

00:17:16.804 --> 00:17:21.070
He's already issued
a warrant for her arrest.

00:17:21.142 --> 00:17:23.303
That sly old dog.

00:17:23.377 --> 00:17:24.742
Access.

00:17:24.812 --> 00:17:27.872
Mail, log file, Armitage.

00:17:27.949 --> 00:17:28.938
Open.

00:17:29.016 --> 00:17:30.711
This is Pluto.

00:17:30.785 --> 00:17:32.514
I'm a Third just like you.

00:17:32.587 --> 00:17:33.713
That's not her.

00:17:33.788 --> 00:17:38.122
I'm sending this message by use
of Armitage's I.D.

00:17:38.192 --> 00:17:42.288
Chris, could you find out where
this mail originated from?

00:17:42.363 --> 00:17:43.728
I'll try.

00:17:47.668 --> 00:17:48.760
Shit.

00:18:03.217 --> 00:18:04.684
C'mon, c'mon...

00:18:04.752 --> 00:18:06.652
c'mon, c'mon.

00:18:08.022 --> 00:18:09.546
Yes, bingo!

00:18:09.624 --> 00:18:12.320
Here is a list
of Thirds from Pluto.

00:18:12.393 --> 00:18:15.021
Pluto? The planet?

00:18:18.866 --> 00:18:22.267
So that's the game.
Hot damn.

00:18:22.336 --> 00:18:24.770
Lieutenant, I've got it!

00:18:24.839 --> 00:18:27.307
Just hold on.
Are you sure?

00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:28.637
Yes, sir.

00:18:28.709 --> 00:18:32.736
I had to take the body apart
to get the result.

00:18:32.813 --> 00:18:36.180
But how?
Can robots really do that?

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.708
Why not?
They can do it technically.

00:18:39.787 --> 00:18:42.187
I'm not talking about that!

00:18:42.256 --> 00:18:44.190
Get me Ross!
- Yes, sir.

00:18:49.897 --> 00:18:51.797
Sylibus.

00:18:51.866 --> 00:18:55.358
I've heard you put a warrant
out for Armitage's arrest.

00:18:55.436 --> 00:18:57.370
That pattern was figured out.

00:18:57.438 --> 00:19:01.033
As we expected,
it's a list of Thirds.

00:19:01.108 --> 00:19:03.838
Pluto is the last one
that's still alive, right?

00:19:03.911 --> 00:19:05.401
How did you know?

00:19:05.479 --> 00:19:07.344
I found out at
the murdered writer's house.

00:19:07.415 --> 00:19:10.873
I'm heading toward dispatch
sector that Chris found.

00:19:10.951 --> 00:19:12.475
I'll call you later.

00:19:12.553 --> 00:19:13.850
There's one more thing.

00:19:13.921 --> 00:19:16.253
We finally learned why
all the Thirds are female.

00:19:16.323 --> 00:19:17.381
What?

00:19:17.458 --> 00:19:20.552
Lavinia Whately was pregnant.

00:19:20.628 --> 00:19:21.720
That's crazy!

00:19:21.796 --> 00:19:25.027
That's a purpose of the Thirds?

00:19:25.099 --> 00:19:27.624
Androids that can reproduce?

00:19:34.709 --> 00:19:36.267
Good morning.

00:19:39.447 --> 00:19:40.573
Good morning.

00:19:40.648 --> 00:19:42.411
Good morning.

00:19:42.483 --> 00:19:44.144
Good morning.

00:19:44.218 --> 00:19:47.210
Who is that strange girl?

00:19:47.288 --> 00:19:49.051
I don't know.

00:19:51.992 --> 00:19:54.324
Good morning.

00:19:54.395 --> 00:19:56.329
Morning!

00:19:56.397 --> 00:19:59.298
Now everyone get in.
Hurry up.

00:19:59.366 --> 00:20:02.426
Class will start shortly.

00:20:02.503 --> 00:20:04.266
Armitage.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:10.408
I used to run home all the time.

00:20:10.478 --> 00:20:15.381
I fell down
and went home crying once.

00:20:15.449 --> 00:20:18.680
MPD has been searching for you.

00:20:22.022 --> 00:20:24.923
You came here to protect
Pluto, right?

00:20:24.992 --> 00:20:26.152
Let's go.

00:20:27.461 --> 00:20:28.485
What?

00:20:28.562 --> 00:20:30.894
I am here to...

00:20:38.506 --> 00:20:41.907
There!
That's him, I'm sure of it.

00:20:41.976 --> 00:20:44.171
But it's a kid!

00:20:45.679 --> 00:20:48.147
How do you do, Pluto?

00:20:48.215 --> 00:20:50.308
Your memory has been locked.

00:20:50.384 --> 00:20:52.682
We're brother and sister.
You've forgotten?

00:20:52.753 --> 00:20:55.313
Uh... sorry.

00:20:55.389 --> 00:20:57.619
By the way, what are you
doing, playing hooky?

00:20:57.691 --> 00:20:58.988
I'm transferring my thoughts...

00:20:59.059 --> 00:21:01.220
to the main memory
at the navigation center.

00:21:02.797 --> 00:21:04.230
What for?

00:21:05.566 --> 00:21:08.399
To make a backup of myself,
obviously.

00:21:13.674 --> 00:21:16.507
I appreciate you sending
the list, Pluto.

00:21:16.577 --> 00:21:18.511
Please don't call me
by my handle.

00:21:18.579 --> 00:21:19.841
It's embarrassing.

00:21:19.914 --> 00:21:22.075
Very well, Julian Moore.

00:21:22.149 --> 00:21:24.674
I never imagined
a child Third...

00:21:24.752 --> 00:21:26.185
and a boy.

00:21:26.253 --> 00:21:31.020
Even the most sophisticated
AL robot cannot grow up.

00:21:31.091 --> 00:21:34.993
I'm a kid forever
unless I'm destroyed.

00:21:35.062 --> 00:21:36.359
Do you know that?

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:40.696
I've heard that I'm the last
model off the Third test line.

00:21:40.768 --> 00:21:43.703
They made me a child,
and a male no less.

00:21:43.771 --> 00:21:45.864
The joke's on me, isn't it?

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:47.965
What is he talking about?
- Well, that's...

00:21:48.042 --> 00:21:50.738
Never mind.

00:21:50.811 --> 00:21:53.905
There's no need for Armitage to
be concerned with it now anyway.

00:21:53.981 --> 00:21:55.539
Hey, you!

00:21:55.616 --> 00:21:58.210
Even though you're Third,
you're just punk!

00:21:58.285 --> 00:22:01.812
Can't you talk to me
more politely?

00:22:01.889 --> 00:22:03.447
What's happened?

00:22:06.994 --> 00:22:07.961
Something's wrong.

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:14.527
It won't stop!

00:22:22.810 --> 00:22:26.610
At this rate,
we'll crash in 20 seconds.

00:22:28.015 --> 00:22:29.812
Hold on tight!

00:22:31.218 --> 00:22:33.743
Hey, what are you doing?

00:22:33.821 --> 00:22:35.152
Just trust me.

00:22:55.409 --> 00:22:56.671
Ross.

00:23:00.381 --> 00:23:03.748
I think my right arm
and some ribs are broken.

00:23:12.493 --> 00:23:13.926
That's the assassin?

00:23:16.397 --> 00:23:17.864
I'll kill you!

00:23:21.702 --> 00:23:23.067
He's fast.

00:23:23.137 --> 00:23:25.537
Ross, Julian,
we gotta run for it!

00:23:25.606 --> 00:23:28.404
Go on. Leave me here.
- No!

00:23:56.470 --> 00:23:58.131
Oh, my God.

00:24:07.982 --> 00:24:09.711
I guess I don't have any choice.

00:24:40.080 --> 00:24:41.274
Thanks, kid.

00:24:41.348 --> 00:24:44.181
If Armitage is killed,
then I'll be the next.

00:24:55.763 --> 00:24:58.527
Impossible!
Who's in Shinora, then?

00:25:00.067 --> 00:25:03.468
I love to watch a girl
throwing up. I just love it.

00:25:03.537 --> 00:25:05.300
You freak!

00:25:16.750 --> 00:25:19.583
I won't let you die alone.

00:25:19.653 --> 00:25:21.917
The other two
will join you later.

00:25:23.090 --> 00:25:24.352
Fucking bastard!

00:25:27.227 --> 00:25:28.660
He's not human!

00:25:29.930 --> 00:25:31.363
Nice right hook...

00:25:31.432 --> 00:25:33.957
but I'm going to
crush the three of you...

00:25:34.034 --> 00:25:35.661
right now!

00:25:44.711 --> 00:25:45.643
What...

00:25:45.712 --> 00:25:47.577
What happened?

00:25:47.648 --> 00:25:49.115
Well, then...

00:25:49.183 --> 00:25:50.810
so long.

00:25:53.287 --> 00:25:56.415
You crazy bitch!
Give me the key!

00:25:56.490 --> 00:25:57.457
No way!

00:26:05.099 --> 00:26:08.591
From this height,
he shouldn't be alive.

00:26:10.971 --> 00:26:13.496
I believed...

00:26:13.574 --> 00:26:15.474
you weren't the killer.

00:26:15.542 --> 00:26:17.237
Security should be here
any minute.

00:26:17.311 --> 00:26:18.437
They'll take you to a hospital.

00:26:18.512 --> 00:26:19.444
Hey...

00:26:19.513 --> 00:26:24.314
Police don't leave
their injured behind.

00:26:30.791 --> 00:26:33.658
You're cold, lady.

00:26:33.727 --> 00:26:34.955
I knew it.

00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:49.372
I am always cold.

00:26:51.311 --> 00:26:53.074
Armitage.

00:29:15.756 --> 00:29:18.224
Why were Thirds killed?

00:29:18.292 --> 00:29:19.725
Why were they made?

00:29:19.793 --> 00:29:21.488
Why are they designed
to reproduce?

00:29:21.561 --> 00:29:22.823
Where is Asakura?

00:29:22.896 --> 00:29:26.195
Is it really D'anclaude
at the hospital in Shinora?

00:29:26.266 --> 00:29:29.497
Right, I have no choice
but to go.

00:29:29.569 --> 00:29:34.404
Armitage III, Episode 3,
"Heart Core."

00:29:34.474 --> 00:29:37.034
D'anclaude,
I'll exterminate you.
